== K10-CORR2-01: what each new control distinguishes ==

Method. The committed payload C is checked out into a detached git worktree; one behaviour at a
time is replaced with the pre-correction behaviour or with a plausible weaker or wrong fix, and
the C4 control file is run. Failing test names are printed in suite order. The repository
checkout is never modified; each ablation is reverted with 'git checkout --' before the next,
and the worktree's final status is printed. These are read-only observations about which
controls can distinguish which implementation; they are not packet validation.

