$ git status --porcelain  # the ablation worktree is restored
?? node_modules
  (node_modules is a symlink this run created so the worktree resolves typescript; untracked, outside the payload)

Reading.

  equality    The reported defect, restored. Four controls reject it: the reproduced family,
              the two-sided direction, the dependency columns now sharing the rule, and the
              diagnostic control, which cannot compare two reports when one is never made.
  blacklist   A correction that forbade the separator byte on the documented side and left the
              comparison alone — the fix the finding explicitly rules out. Three controls
              reject it. The decisive one is the two-sided control: the enforced member spells
              the separator and the documented members do not, so no blacklist on the document
              can fire and the old rendering still collides, which is silence about a false
              relation. The merge family also rejects it, because it reports a byte rather
              than naming the relation and its two sizes.
  diagnostic  The equality is correct and the message is not. Seven controls reject it; three
              are pre-existing mutated-document controls whose expected text this packet
              updated to the unambiguous rendering.
  cardinality Members compared without sizes. Dropping a member that sorts last leaves a
              prefix that elementwise comparison accepts, so the dropped-member controls
              (which drop the last as well as the first) and the pre-existing dropped-subpath
              control are what reject it.
  membership  Sizes compared without members. The swapped-root, replaced-root and
              same-size/different-members controls reject it.
  set         The pre-correction representation. Five controls reject it on shape. The honest
              limit: a *de-duplicating array* passes every control, because the cardinality
              collapse a Set could cause is unreachable while decodeCodeSpanList rejects a
              token repeated inside one cell. Removing that coupling is defence in depth,
              recorded as such, and is not a reproduced defect.
